        <dc:title>Make Me</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Child, Lee" opf:role="aut">Lee Child</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (1.48.0) [http://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2015-09-07T23:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>&lt;b&gt;#1 &lt;i&gt;NEW YORK TIMES &lt;/i&gt;BESTSELLER&lt;li&gt;NAMED ONE OF THE BEST BOOKS OF THE YEAR BY &lt;i&gt;LOS ANGELES TIMES&lt;/i&gt; AND &lt;i&gt;THE GUARDIAN&lt;/i&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stephen King calls Jack Reacher "the coolest continuing series character"--and now he's back in this masterly new thriller from Lee Child.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; &lt;i&gt;"Why is this town called Mother's Rest?"&lt;/i&gt; That's all Reacher wants to know. But no one will tell him. It's a tiny place hidden in a thousand square miles of wheat fields, with a railroad stop, and sullen and watchful people, and a worried woman named Michelle Chang, who mistakes him for someone else: her missing partner in a private investigation she thinks must have started small and then turned lethal.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Reacher has no particular place to go, and all the time in the world to get there, and there's something about Chang . . . so he teams up with her and starts to ask around. He thinks: How bad can this thing be? But before long he's plunged into a desperate race through LA, Chicago,...</dc:description>
        <dc:publisher>Random House Publishing Group</dc:publisher>
        <dc:language>eng</dc:language>
